# Force LF for migration SQL and the migration runner itself, regardless of
# a contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a plain
# `git checkout` on Windows can silently rewrite these files from LF to
# CRLF, which changes their exact bytes without changing their content —
# and this project's migration checksums (run_migrations.py, added for
# drift detection) hash exact file bytes. Confirmed live (Sept 2026):
# tampering with 0003_add_soft_delete_columns.sql was correctly detected,
# but reverting it via `git checkout --` on Windows still failed a
# checksum check afterward, purely from LF->CRLF conversion on checkout.
*.sql text eol=lf
migrations/run_migrations.py text eol=lf
